{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Input Device.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Input Device.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"input device input device","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Input Device.md","fileName":"Input Device.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Input Device","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Interaction Technique","Degrees of Freedom","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Input Device.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Input Device.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"input device input device","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Input Device.md","fileName":"Input Device.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Input Device","heading":"Input Device","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An input device is a physical device that allows communication from a user to a computer. It is the hardware used to capture an action; the [[Interaction Technique]] supplies the software mapping that turns the captured data into an effect in the system.\n\nInput can be discrete, such as a button value, continuous, such as a stream of positions, or a combination of both. Important characteristics include [[Degrees of Freedom]], data frequency, whether measurements are absolute or relative, and whether the sensor must be held or worn. A device should be selected together with the task and interaction technique because one device may map naturally to one task and poorly to another.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Interaction Technique","Degrees of Freedom","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"i